<dd id="mwvA">which lands in the dual projective space.</dd></dl>
<ul id="mwvQ"><li id="mwvg">The dual variety of a point <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt79" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"(&apos;&apos;a&apos;&apos;&lt;sub>0&lt;/sub> : ... : &apos;&apos;a&lt;sub>n&lt;/sub>&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>(<i>a</i><sub>0</sub><span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>: ...<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>: <i>a<sub>n</sub></i>)</span> is the hyperplane</li></ul>
<dl id="mwwA"><dd id="mwwQ"><dl id="mwwg"><dd id="mwww"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt80" id="mwxA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"a_0x_0+\\ldots +a_nx_n=0."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle a_{0}x_{0}+\ldots +a_{n}x_{n}=0.}">
